    "Condition : 1 - The proposed works as shown on the plans constitute permitted development as defined by Schedule 2, Part 1, Class B of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) Order 1995(as amended).\r\n\r\nINFORMATIVE\r\n\r\nThe proposed roof extension with dimensions generally 5.2m wide by 3.8m deep with a height of 2.5m for the proposed dormer extension, and 3.8m wide, 1.8m deep and 2.6m high for the rear projection that adds a total of 38.7m3 to the volume of the existing dwellinghouse, as shown on drawings received by Council on 4 December 2002, is lawful within the meaning of Section 191 and 192 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 and therefore does not require planning permission."
